%% DM26-0670

%% Runtime attestation, slice C: the process itself (runtime-attestation.md, "Runtime attestation of the process", "The node sensor";
%% outlined, to be planned when slices A and B are built, after the OpenAPI and GitLab agents are on the builder). All designed, nothing built.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Ag as An agent's process
    participant Lock as Its builder actor
    participant Sensor as Node sensor (one per node)
    participant Att as Attestation agent
    participant CA as Credentials agent

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Ag,Lock: DESIGNED: before it parses any untrusted input, irreversibly
    Ag->>Lock: start
    Lock->>Ag: apply seccomp (no execve, ptrace or memfd_create, no new executable memory) and Landlock
    end

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Sensor,Att: DESIGNED: evidence from outside the process. What a process says about itself is worthless
    loop on a schedule
        Sensor->>Sensor: read the container's cgroup, and the agent's Seccomp and NoNewPrivs state
        Sensor-)Att: the processes it found, and that state, over Cassini
        Att->>Lock: a fresh challenge, over Cassini
        alt it answers in time
            Lock-->>Att: the answer
        else missed or stale
            Att->>Att: the instance has lapsed
        end
        Att->>Att: a process that is not the agent, or the lock not in force: the instance has lapsed
    end
    Att-)CA: a lapsed instance: acting on it is the body guard's, as in slice B
    end
